WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.367
A threat

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.535
of, quote, catastrophic consequences

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:03.703
for the United States

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.038
from a top Chinese Communist

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.439
Party official today

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.841
after a series of high profile

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:08.842
diplomatic squabbles,

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:09.876
China's new foreign

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.478
minister drew a red line

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:12.312
with the United States

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.347
over the issue of Taiwan.

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.383
And he defended Beijing's

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.418
relationship with Moscow, Russia.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.686
CNN's Selina Wang

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.321
went to the National People's Congress

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:21.821
in Beijing

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.357
to find obstacles for journalists

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.759
covering the foreign minister's

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:28.561
tightly controlled debut

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.064
Thousands of government delegates across

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.232
China are gathering

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.501
for the biggest annual political meeting

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.336
known as the two sessions.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.170
It's the first

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:37.904
since China

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:40.040
abandoned its zero COVID policy.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.175
But reporters covering

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.010
the event are still stuck

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.345
in a coated bubble

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.946
required to stay overnight

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.348
at a quarantine hotel

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:50.517
and get an onsite PCR test.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.585
We just left the quarantine hotel.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.054
We're now headed to the venue.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.189
Everything is highly controlled.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.290
The foreign media bus

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.325
gets dropped off at Tiananmen Square.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:00.960
It is very rare for journalists

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.228
to get access to this.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:02.896
As you can see, though,

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.531
there's heavy security.

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.965
There are guards everywhere.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:06.633
Normally

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.701
the two sessions is the rare chance

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.437
for media to get up and close

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:11.905
to China's top leadership

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:12.572
right here

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.106
on the steps

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.274
of the Great Hall of the People.

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:16.476
This is normally where you will see media

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:17.610
trying to doorstop

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.179
off the top leadership.

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.914
But as you can see,

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.682
this year, we,

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.384
the media were completely separate

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:25.418
from the rest of the leaders

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.054
The two

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:28.922
sessions is a

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.790
carefully choreographed event.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.358
The new government shake up Scott,

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.427
a rubber stamp parliament will vote on

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.463
has one unifying goal

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.230
to strength

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.131
Xi Jinping

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.266
and the ruling Communist Party's power.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.302
And the COVID restrictions

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.403
are the perfect tool

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.972
for Beijing to control the message.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.741
So media has to apply to get access

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:49.776
to specific events.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.945
Were not granted approval to all of them.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.012
And this is the media

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:55.181
area inside the Great Hall of the People.

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:55.882
As you can see,

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:56.983
it's pretty empty

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.619
so it's clearly not an issue of capacity.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.488
Some of the events during the week

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.989
long meeting allow select

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.390
reporter questions,

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.692
including Ching Gong's

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:06.993
first press conference

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.963
as China's new foreign minister.

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.764
He said that conflict with the U.S.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:12.866
is inevitable

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:15.268
if Washington does not change course.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.804
Qin Gang called Washington's approach

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:20.640
a reckless gamble, accused the U.S.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.909
of creating a crisis over Taiwan,

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:25.512
defended China's partnership with Russia

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:26.946
as imperative

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:27.480
and said

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.816
it has not supplied weapons to Russia

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.217
or Ukraine.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.386
See you at the two sessions.

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:34.988
Meanwhile, Chinese state media

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:35.822
is portraying

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.123
the legislative meeting

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.258
as an open event

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:40.426
where journalists can freely operate.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:43.229
Sri Lanka. Hi, I'm from Luke News.

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.697
It's an amazing country.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.766
The assemblies also offered journalists

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:47.567
the opportunity

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.469
to put questions to the Chinese

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.604
premier and ministers.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.306
What's the deal like? Let me 80.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:54.541
But under these controls

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.542
spontaneous run

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:56.609
ins with top leaders

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:57.443
like the Premier

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.812
and ministers are out of reach.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.648
But after today's meeting ended,

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:02.715
we had a few minutes

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.083
to approach some delegates,

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:04.617
which are a

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.853
curated group of local representative

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:08.988
This delegate is part of the Duong

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.590
ethnic minority from the south

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.192
western Gwangju province.

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:13.993
She says this is her first time

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.228
attending the Congress

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.397
and she feels happy to see her motherland

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.898
becoming stronger.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.133
The rest of the delegates

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.167
quickly rush out

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.469
before we have a chance to approach them.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.437
The question

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.406
is how much of these COVID controls

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.741
will remain in post-pandemic China?

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:32.245
It limited access even more to China's

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.080
already extremely opaque

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.548
political machine.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.283
This much is clear

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.451
the communist leadership

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:40.587
only wants the world to see one

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:42.188
narrative from China.

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:45.091
That is the image of unity, strength

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:46.326
and victory.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.232
Jake, those COVID

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.833
restrictions were so surprising

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:55.235
considering the country has already

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:56.502
completely opened up.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.604
So it really seems like

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:58.938
those COVID controls

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.006
were really just an excuse

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:02.041
to restrict press access.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:02.675
Now, this year's

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.110
two sessions is significant

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.912
because it is the first after

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:06.980
Xi Jinping secured

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.181
that precedent, shattering

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:10.416
third term as party chief last October.

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:12.452
Now, during this political event, he's

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:14.087
now set to get an unprecedented

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.755
third term as president

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:17.690
It is a largely ceremonial title,

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.891
but it is significant.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.193
We'll also see a new slate

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.027
to aid government

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:23.196
leaders and institutional reforms made.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:24.864
All of that is going to increase

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:27.066
the communist party's grip. And and.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.301
This was the foreign minister's

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:30.036
first time front and center like this.

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.471
What did you make of his comments?

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:34.941
Yeah, it's interesting.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.010
This was a very fiery and combative

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.378
press conference before this.

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:40.480
He was actually the Chinese ambassador

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.114
to the US.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:41.748
He's known

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.549
as this very accomplished

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.018
and measured diplomat.

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:46.486
So very significant here

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:48.888
that he made such strong comments.

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:49.455
At one point,

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.923
he even made a show of reading

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.358
from a copy of the Constitution

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:52.859
of the People's

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:53.693
Republic of China

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:55.595
to emphasize Beijing's claims

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:56.763
that the self-governing

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:57.930
democracy of Taiwan

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.600
is part of its, quote, sacred territory.

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.135
He also said the Taiwan issue

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.003
is the bedrock of Sino-U.S.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.605
relations and that, quote,

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:08.408
the red line that must not be crossed.

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:09.676
Now, this press conference

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:11.611
came amid reports of a potential meeting

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.845
between Taiwan's president

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.147
Tsai Ing Wen and U.S.

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:16.449
House Speaker Kevin McCarthy in April.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:17.483
Regardless of where

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:18.251
that meeting is held,

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:19.152
the Financial Times said

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.820
it could be held in the US.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:21.721
This is going to draw

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.056
the ire of Beijing it's

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:24.223
going to increase already

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:26.092
tense relations Jake.

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:26.392
All right.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.360
Selina Wang in Beijing,

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.328
thank you so much.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:29.696
I want to bring in Republican Senator

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:31.864
Dan Sullivan of Alaska.

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:32.365
We should note

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:33.933
of course, by the way, that Xi Jinping,

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:35.702
when he's reelected, it's by the

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:36.969
the National People's Congress.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.371
It's not by the people

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:39.238
the way that we do it here

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:40.440
in the United States.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.307
Senator, how

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:42.408
how does the United States

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.109
transition

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:44.110
from this increasingly

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.546
combative relationship with China

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:50.049
into into one that is less hostile?

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:51.184
And what was your reaction

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:53.519
to the new foreign minister's comments?

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:54.754
Well, I know the foreign minister

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:56.923
and I think his comments

00:05:56.923 --> 00:05:58.658
about the United States

00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:01.027
needing to pump the brakes

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:01.561
or there's

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:03.663
going to be some kind of conflict.

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:04.330
I think

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.998
China, the Chinese Communist

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:06.933
Party,

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.034
Jake, is the one

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:09.802
that needs to pump the brakes.

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.471
Look at what they've done in terms

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:13.306
of aggressive actions

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:14.674
in the last two years.

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:15.808
I mean, obviously,

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:17.777
the pandemic is a huge issue.

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:19.512
But with regard to its neighbors,

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:20.747
whether it literally

00:06:20.747 --> 00:06:21.914
was a shooting war

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:22.515
on the border

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:23.549
with India,

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:25.718
the crushing of any kind of liberty

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:27.620
and democracy in Taiwan,

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.355
the crushing of what's going on

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:30.690
with regard to the weakness

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:33.793
in economic

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:37.230
embargo and coercion against Australia,

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:38.998
in the aggressive actions

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:40.800
that they take almost daily

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.335
in the Taiwan Strait

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:43.770
and the South China Sea.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.539
That's just in the last two years,

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:48.574
or this is a regime

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:51.244
that is showing very aggressive actions

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:52.712
to its neighbors

00:06:52.712 --> 00:06:54.180
and all around the world.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:54.981
And I think

00:06:54.981 --> 00:06:57.049
if anyone needs to pump the brakes

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.251
on their actions, it's

00:06:58.251 --> 00:07:01.421
the Chinese Communist Party, not America.

00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:02.989
On the subject of Taiwan,

00:07:02.989 --> 00:07:04.323
there are reports that Taiwan's

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:05.291
president is going to meet

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:06.058
with Republican House

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:08.394
Speaker Kevin McCarthy in April.

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:09.695
China's Foreign

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:10.963
Ministry have warned McCarthy

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:12.498
not to visit Taiwan,

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:13.232
so it's possible

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:13.666
the meeting might

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:15.134
take place in California.

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:15.902
We don't know.

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:16.769
Either way, Beijing

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:18.571
is likely going to react.

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:20.606
What do you think about McCarthy meeting

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:23.209
the president of Taiwan?

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:24.844
Is that appropriate?

00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:26.012
Do you support it?

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:27.113
We should remind people that

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:29.015
that then Speaker Nancy Pelosi

00:07:29.015 --> 00:07:30.049
visited Taiwan,

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:30.683
and that was also

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:31.818
considered poking the bear.

00:07:33.052 --> 00:07:33.686
Well, you remember

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:35.655
when Nancy Pelosi visited Taiwan,

00:07:35.655 --> 00:07:39.892
I actually led a statement of over 40

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:40.626
I think it was 40

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:41.627
us senators,

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:44.831
a bipartisan group of senators that said

00:07:45.131 --> 00:07:47.967
we should support Pelosi's visit.

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:48.468
Actually, I'm

00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:50.403
sorry, on Pelosi's visit,

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:52.472
it was just Republicans, ironically.

00:07:52.472 --> 00:07:54.607
I actually think if the speaker,

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:56.108
the number three

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:58.311
elected official in our government,

00:07:58.311 --> 00:07:59.846
wants to visit Taiwan,

00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:01.614
that that individual

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:03.649
should be able to do so.

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:04.584
And we shouldn't

00:08:04.584 --> 00:08:06.385
let the Chinese Communist Party

00:08:06.385 --> 00:08:08.955
dictate where elected American officials

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:09.755
can travel.

